§ `String index probe`
-- Exercises the index-carrying string builtins STRINGLENGTH / INDEXOF /
-- CHARAT / SUBSTRING. The curated cases are branch-crossing on
-- code-UNIT vs code-POINT semantics: jl4-service (Data.Text) counts by
-- Unicode code point, while naive JS string ops count by UTF-16 code
-- unit — any astral-plane char (e.g. 😀 U+1F600, a surrogate pair in
-- JS) makes the two disagree. SUBSTRING cases additionally cross on the
-- third argument being a LENGTH (Text.take len . Text.drop start), not
-- an end index as JS .substring would read it.
--
-- NOTE: the first @export in a §-sectioned file is emitted as a helper
-- (frontend/schema quirk), so the first DECIDE below is a SACRIFICIAL
-- throwaway; everything we actually curate cases for comes after it.

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@export
DECIDE probePrime IF x

@export
GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE strLen IS STRINGLENGTH s

@export
GIVEN h IS A STRING
      n IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE idxOf IS INDEXOF h n

@export
GIVEN s IS A STRING
      i IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE chAt IS CHARAT s i

@export
GIVEN s IS A STRING
      i IS A NUMBER
      j IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE subStr IS SUBSTRING s i j
